{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Add-On Import Management.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Add-On Import Management.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender add on import management blender add on import management","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Add-On Import Management.md","fileName":"Blender Add-On Import Management.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Add-On Import Management","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Add-On Development Workflow]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Add-On Development Workflow","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Add-On Import Management.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Add-On Import Management.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender add on import management blender add on import management","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Add-On Import Management.md","fileName":"Blender Add-On Import Management.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Add-On Import Management","heading":"Blender Add-On Import Management","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A multi-file Blender add-on must distinguish its first package import from later development reloads. On first load, a sibling module is imported relative to the package; on reload, the already known module is explicitly refreshed so edits become part of the running add-on.\n\nThe source uses the presence of `bpy` in local names to select these paths and imports `bpy` afterward. The exact protocol reflects its Blender and Python version, but the broader issue persists: module caches can preserve old code unless the development lifecycle deliberately refreshes dependencies.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Add-On Development Workflow","blend